From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 108/108] net: mtk_eth_soc: optimize MT7621 FE PSE SRAM thresholds & enforce GDMA1/GDMA2 HW checksum

Fixes the MT7621AT Frame Engine (0x1e100000) Packet Switch Engine (PSE) free
page starvation under heavy non-WED `WAN -> 5 GHz Wi-Fi` bursts and guarantees
hardware IPv4/TCP/UDP checksum generation & verification on both GDMA1 (LAN
TRGMII) and GDMA2 (WAN RGMII).

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3410,6 +3410,9 @@ static int mtk_hw_init(struct mtk_eth *eth, bool reset)
 		val = mtk_r32(eth, MTK_GDMA_FWD_CFG(i));
 
 		/* setup the forward port to send frame to PDMA */
 		val &= ~0xffff;
+		/* NexSilicon Fix: Enforce Hardware ICS/TCS/UCS Checksum Offload on GDMA1 & GDMA2 */
+		val |= MTK_GDMA_ICS_EN | MTK_GDMA_TCS_EN | MTK_GDMA_UCS_EN;
 
 		mtk_w32(eth, val, MTK_GDMA_FWD_CFG(i));
 	}
